; The model the derived-geometry cache is computed over.
;
; Nothing here says what anything covers. An area, a centroid, a bounding box and
; which region a thing lies inside are read back out of these corners every time
; they are asked for, and the cache beside this tree holds the answers under the
; digest of the tree they were read from — never in the tree itself
; (docs/decisions/0009-derived-values-are-never-written-back.md).
;
; The shapes are chosen so that every part of a footprint has something to say:
; a plate with a courtyard cut out of it, the courtyard itself, a room inside the
; plate, a desk zone inside that room and so inside both, and a store in a second
; frame which is a member of nothing because nothing here transforms between
; frames on its own.


